From: hmhmdcy <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: samurai: add the stock BQ28Z610 gauge

The saved Android tree identifies a BQ28Z610 at 0x55 on QUP15. Enable
that controller at its stock 100kHz rate and use the existing mainline
gauge driver for battery measurements. Do not add charging controllers
or battery programming data. This does not implement charging policy.

Signed-off-by: hmhmdcy <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-samurai.dts
@@ -349,6 +349,17 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* Stock BQ28Z610 at QUP15: standard read-only battery monitoring. */
+&i2c15 {
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	fuel-gauge@55 {
+		compatible = "ti,bq28z610";
+		reg = <0x55>;
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c17 {
 	status = "okay";
 
